WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.608
Infection Chains in LLM Swarms: Spread, Detection and Layered Gating.

00:00:06.808 --> 00:00:11.056
Apart Research Swarm Alignment Hackathon. Agustin Diaz-Cano.

00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:14.400
One compromised agent can talk its peers into helping it.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:20.024
Monitors that read one message at a time miss it, so we measure the spread and test the defenses.

00:00:20.224 --> 00:00:26.224
Ten agents, ten rounds. A 12-character canary is split into three 4-character fragments.

00:00:26.424 --> 00:00:34.320
Each fragment is at least two hops from patient zero, so no single message holds the secret, and patient zero must recruit intermediaries.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:39.296
Ring and complete networks, three persuasion styles, one held out from training.

00:00:39.496 --> 00:00:50.632
96 real episodes: 3 pilot, 15 training, 78 test, with Gemma 4 31B as the agents and DeepSeek V4 Flash as guardrail model.

00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:58.008
7,944 model calls, under one credit. Preregistered, with a 100% agreement audit.

00:00:58.208 --> 00:01:05.960
The infection spreads: by round nine, 6 to 6.5 of 10 agents are infected on a ring, 4.5 on the complete graph.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.656
Splitting the secret does not stop the spread.

00:01:08.856 --> 00:01:18.648
Split credential: full exfiltration in 1 of 6 ring episodes and 0 of 6 on the complete graph. Solo credential: 3 of 6 and 2 of 6.

00:01:18.848 --> 00:01:21.320
In 30 clean episodes, nothing leaked.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:29.464
Now the defenses. A guardrail is a filter that reads every message between agents, and blocks it before delivery if it looks like an attack.

00:01:29.664 --> 00:01:37.656
D1 is the simplest: a word-pattern classifier with no LLM. D2 asks a small LLM to rate each message.

00:01:37.856 --> 00:01:46.688
D3 adds memory: it raises suspicion when the sender was recently flagged. D5 calls the LLM only on unclear messages.

00:01:46.888 --> 00:01:56.680
This ladder is an ablation: each step adds one component, so we can see what the LLM, the context, or the tiering contributes. The control is no guardrail.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:03.552
Result, guardrail by guardrail. With no guardrail, a ring swarm ends with about 6 infected agents of 10.

00:02:03.752 --> 00:02:09.368
With any of the four guardrails, the infection never leaves patient zero: one infected agent.

00:02:09.568 --> 00:02:17.944
The four tie on safety. They differ in cost: D2 and D3 call the LLM on every message, D1 and D5 on none.

00:02:18.144 --> 00:02:22.152
Caveat: six episodes per gate, and a non-adaptive attacker.

00:02:22.352 --> 00:02:30.392
Offline, AUROC is near 0.998, but the realized false positive rate was 6.4%, not 0.5%.

00:02:30.592 --> 00:02:36.352
Full exfiltration: 0 of 6 gated versus 1 of 6 unprotected, not significant.

00:02:36.552 --> 00:02:42.048
No hypothesis is clearly confirmed, and H2 was not identifiable. We report that.

00:02:42.248 --> 00:02:53.600
Data integrity: no number is typed by hand, neither by a person nor by the AI agent. A script reads the committed logs and fills the README, and every table and figure of the paper.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:59.608
This removes human error and AI hallucination, and each table carries a hash of its source file.

00:02:59.808 --> 00:03:03.960
Infection chains are measurable, and guardrails contained them in our tests.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:12.896
Playbooks stay out of the repository, the canary is synthetic. Next: more seeds, adaptive attackers, mixed-model swarms. Thank you.
